<title>USA: SunTrust files $600 mln shelf.</title>
<headline>SunTrust files $600 mln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>SunTrust Banks Inc filed a shelf offering on Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $600 million in debt securities and preferred stock to be offered by SunTrust Capital I and SunTrust Capital II.</p>
<p>The Atlanta-based bank holding company said each of the Trusts will use the proceeds they receive from selling preferred shares to purchase subordinated debt securities from the company. The company said it will use the proceeds from the sale of the subordinated debt for general corporate needs, including investments in its subsidiaries.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
